## Development

See [CONTRIBUTING.md](CONTRIBUTING.md). In short:

```sh
uv sync                  # a .venv with the package (editable) and the dev tools
uv run pytest            # the tests, in parallel and in random order
uv run ruff check .      # lint; `uv run ruff format .` formats
{% if use_ty %}
uv run ty check          # type check
{% endif %}
{% if flavour == "notebooks" %}
uv run scripts/run_notebooks.py   # execute every notebook headless into notebooks/executed/
{% endif %}
uvx prek install         # run the git hooks on every commit (`uvx prek run --all-files` runs them now)
```

CI runs the tests on Python {{ python_versions.split() | join(", ") }}{% if flavour == "notebooks" %}, executes every notebook{% endif %}, runs
the git hooks, checks the dependencies with pip-audit and runs OpenSSF Scorecard, all through
[Rakiura-Inc's shared workflows](https://github.com/Rakiura-Inc/.github). Renovate keeps the
dependencies, hooks and workflows current.
{% if flavour == "library" %}

## Releasing

1. Bump `__version__` in `src/{{ package_name }}/_version.py` and add the entry to `CHANGELOG.md`.
2. Merge to `main`, then tag that commit and push the tag: `git tag v0.1.0 && git push origin v0.1.0`.
3. The Release workflow builds the wheel and sdist, records their build provenance and attaches
   them to a GitHub Release. Check a download with
   `gh attestation verify <file> --repo {{ github_org }}/{{ project_name }}`.
